<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>fileTypes</key>
	<array>
		<string>pyfun</string>
	</array>
	<key>name</key>
	<string>Pyfun</string>
	<key>patterns</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#comments</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#strings</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#computation-expressions</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#declarations</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#keywords</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#constants</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#numbers</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#types</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#operators</string>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>repository</key>
	<dict>
		<key>comments</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>#.*$</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>comment.line.number-sign.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<key>computation-expressions</key>
		<dict>
			<key>comment</key>
			<string>The four built-in CE builders, only when opening a block.</string>
			<key>match</key>
			<string>\b(async|seq|result|option)\b(?=\s*\{)</string>
			<key>name</key>
			<string>keyword.other.computation.pyfun</string>
		</dict>
		<key>constants</key>
		<dict>
			<key>match</key>
			<string>\b(true|false)\b</string>
			<key>name</key>
			<string>constant.language.pyfun</string>
		</dict>
		<key>declarations</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>captures</key>
					<dict>
						<key>1</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>keyword.declaration.pyfun</string>
						</dict>
						<key>2</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>storage.modifier.mutable.pyfun</string>
						</dict>
						<key>3</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>entity.name.function.pyfun</string>
						</dict>
					</dict>
					<key>comment</key>
					<string>`let mut name` — `mut` is the mutability escape hatch (opt-out of immutable-by-default). Honest scope (it *is* a storage modifier) + a `.mutable` tail the extension pins to keyword pink via configurationDefaults, matching Rust's `mut`.</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(let)\b\s+(mut)\b\s*([a-z_][A-Za-z0-9_']*)?</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>captures</key>
					<dict>
						<key>1</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>keyword.declaration.pyfun</string>
						</dict>
						<key>2</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>storage.modifier.pyfun</string>
						</dict>
						<key>3</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>keyword.control.pyfun</string>
						</dict>
						<key>4</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>entity.name.function.pyfun</string>
						</dict>
					</dict>
					<key>comment</key>
					<string>`let [pure] name` / `let! name` — colour the bound name as a function/binding. `pure` is an encouraged effect assertion, so it stays a neutral storage modifier.</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(let)\b(?:\s+(pure)\b)?\s*(!)?\s*([a-z_][A-Za-z0-9_']*)?</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>comment</key>
					<string>`extern` — the untyped-on-the-Python-side FFI boundary, effectful-by-default; an escape hatch. Honest keyword scope + a `.extern` tail the extension pins to the same keyword pink as `mut`.</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(extern)\b</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>keyword.other.extern.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>comment</key>
					<string>Other binding/declaration keywords (benign). `import` brings in a module (§6.1) and `as` names an as-pattern.</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(fun|type|opaque|measure|module|import|as)\b</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>keyword.declaration.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<key>keywords</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>comment</key>
					<string>Control-flow keywords. `case` is a match arm (DESIGN.md §7.2); `match e:` / `case pat [if guard]: body`. `elif` is sugar for `else if`. `with` now only introduces a record update `{ p with x = 3 }`.</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(if|then|else|elif|match|case|with|return|yield|do|try)\b(!)?</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>keyword.control.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(and|or|not)\b</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>keyword.operator.logical.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<key>numbers</key>
		<dict>
			<key>captures</key>
			<dict>
				<key>1</key>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>constant.numeric.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
				<key>2</key>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>storage.type.unit.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
			</dict>
			<key>comment</key>
			<string>Integer/float literals, with an optional adjacent unit-of-measure annotation (e.g. 5&lt;m&gt;, 3.0&lt;m/s^2&gt;). The unit must touch the digits — matching Pyfun's lexer rule that distinguishes 5&lt;m&gt; from 5 &lt; m.</string>
			<key>match</key>
			<string>\b(\d+(?:\.\d+)?)(&lt;[^&lt;&gt;]+&gt;)?</string>
		</dict>
		<key>operators</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\|&gt;</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>keyword.operator.pipe.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>comment</key>
					<string>`&lt;-` reassignment — the act of mutation. Honest operator scope + a `.mutation` tail pinned to the same keyword pink as `mut`.</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>&lt;-</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>keyword.operator.mutation.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>-&gt;</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>keyword.operator.arrow.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>==|!=|&lt;=|&gt;=|&lt;|&gt;</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>keyword.operator.comparison.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>//|[+\-*/]</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>keyword.operator.arithmetic.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>=</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>keyword.operator.assignment.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\|</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>punctuation.separator.pattern.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<key>strings</key>
		<dict>
			<key>begin</key>
			<string>"</string>
			<key>end</key>
			<string>"</string>
			<key>name</key>
			<string>string.quoted.double.pyfun</string>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\\.</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>constant.character.escape.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<key>types</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>comment</key>
					<string>Built-in collection modules used as a namespace (before a dot).</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(List|Set|Map|Option|Result|Seq|Async)\b(?=\.)</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>entity.name.namespace.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>comment</key>
					<string>Type names and data constructors: any upper-case-led identifier.</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_']*\b</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>entity.name.type.pyfun</string>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</dict>
	<key>scopeName</key>
	<string>source.pyfun</string>
	<key>uuid</key>
	<string>6c1f3b52-7d3e-4c1a-9a0e-5f2b8d1e4a70</string>
</dict>
</plist>
